[{"label":"One identity, two palettes","html":"<article class=\"paper\" data-variant=\"minimal\" aria-labelledby=\"pd-title\">\n  <header class=\"paper-hero\">\n    <p class=\"paper-venue\"\n      ><span class=\"badge\" data-variant=\"secondary\">Short paper</span>\n      <label class=\"swap\" data-variant=\"rotate\" id=\"pd-mode\">\n        <input type=\"checkbox\" aria-label=\"Dark mode\" />\n        <span class=\"swap-on\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i data-lucide=\"moon\"></i></span>\n        <span class=\"swap-off\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i data-lucide=\"sun\"></i></span>\n      </label>\n    </p>\n    <h1 class=\"paper-title\" id=\"pd-title\">One Identity, Two Palettes</h1>\n    <ul class=\"paper-authors\"\n      ><li>Aron Homberg</li\n      ><li>Claude</li></ul\n    >\n  </header>\n\n  <section class=\"paper-abstract\" aria-labelledby=\"pd-abstract\">\n    <h2 id=\"pd-abstract\">Abstract</h2>\n    <p\n      >A theme that is round in light mode and square in dark mode is two themes. defuss-shadcn treats light and dark as\n      two palettes of one identity: every preset declares its radius in both blocks with the same value, a verifier gate\n      fails the build otherwise, and the reading pairs reach 4.5:1 in both modes.</p\n    >\n  </section>\n\n  <nav class=\"paper-toc\" aria-labelledby=\"pd-toc\">\n    <h2 id=\"pd-toc\">Contents</h2>\n    <ol>\n      <li\n        ><a href=\"#pd-s1\"><span class=\"paper-num\">1&nbsp;</span>The shape stays</a></li\n      >\n      <li\n        ><a href=\"#pd-s2\"><span class=\"paper-num\">2&nbsp;</span>The switch</a></li\n      >\n      <li\n        ><a href=\"#pd-cite\"><span class=\"paper-num\">·&nbsp;</span>Citation and references</a></li\n      >\n    </ol>\n  </nav>\n\n  <section class=\"paper-section\" aria-labelledby=\"pd-s1\">\n    <h2 id=\"pd-s1\"><span class=\"paper-num\">1&nbsp;</span>The shape stays</h2>\n    <p>Five of the 43 presets, as their files declare them:</p>\n    <figure class=\"paper-table\">\n      <table class=\"table\">\n        <thead\n          ><tr\n            ><th scope=\"col\">Preset</th><th scope=\"col\" data-num>Radius, light / dark</th\n            ><th scope=\"col\" data-num>Text contrast, light / dark</th></tr\n          ></thead\n        >\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Claude</td><td data-num>0.5rem / 0.5rem</td><td data-num>10.98 / 8.33</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Catppuccin</td><td data-num>0.35rem / 0.35rem</td><td data-num>7.06 / 12.14</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Notebook</td><td data-num>0.625rem / 0.625rem</td><td data-num>10.80 / 10.33</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Doom 64</td><td data-num>0px / 0px</td><td data-num>10.26 / 13.18</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Neo Brutalism</td><td data-num>0px / 0px</td><td data-num>21.00 / 21.00</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <figcaption class=\"paper-table-caption\"><b>Table 1.</b> Foreground on background, WCAG 2 ratio.</figcaption>\n    </figure>\n  </section>\n\n  <section class=\"paper-section\" aria-labelledby=\"pd-s2\">\n    <h2 id=\"pd-s2\"><span class=\"paper-num\">2&nbsp;</span>The switch</h2>\n    <p\n      >The Swap is a label around a checkbox; CSS turns the sun into the moon. The page listens to the checkbox and\n      toggles <code>.dark</code> on the root element - the token file's dark block matches it, so every component\n      follows without a second stylesheet.</p\n    >\n  </section>\n  <section class=\"paper-bibtex\" aria-labelledby=\"pd-cite\">\n    <h2 id=\"pd-cite\">Citation and references</h2>\n    <figure class=\"bibtex\" data-formats=\"bibtex apa mla ieee\" aria-label=\"Cite this paper\">\n      <figcaption>Cite this paper</figcaption>\n      <pre><code class=\"bibtex-source\">@techreport{homberg2026darkmode,\n  title = {One Identity, Two Palettes},\n  author = {Homberg, Aron and Claude},\n  institution = {defuss},\n  year = {2026},\n  month = oct,\n  url = {https://shadcn.defuss.org/papers/paper-dark-mode.html}\n}</code></pre>\n    </figure>\n    <figure class=\"bibtex\" data-formats=\"ieee apa bibtex\" data-format=\"ieee\" aria-label=\"References\">\n      <figcaption>References</figcaption>\n      <pre><code class=\"bibtex-source\">@misc{w3c2023wcag22,\n  author = {{W3C}},\n  title = {Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2},\n  year = {2023},\n  howpublished = {W3C Recommendation},\n  url = {https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/}\n}\n\n@misc{shadcn2023ui,\n  author = {shadcn},\n  title = {shadcn/ui},\n  year = {2023},\n  url = {https://ui.shadcn.com}\n}\n\n@misc{homberg2026defussshadcn,\n  author = {Homberg, Aron},\n  title = {defuss-shadcn: shadcn-style components as semantic HTML},\n  year = {2026},\n  howpublished = {GitHub},\n  url = {https://github.com/kyr0/defuss-shadcn}\n}</code></pre>\n    </figure>\n  </section>\n</article>\n","individual":false}]
